{"total_count":1126,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/commits/fdd28399dc9da913a12983b178290303c14eae81","sha":"fdd28399dc9da913a12983b178290303c14eae81","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0NjU2MDA5NzU6ZmRkMjgzOTlkYzlkYTkxM2ExMjk4M2IxNzgyOTAzMDNjMTRlYWU4MQ==","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/fdd28399dc9da913a12983b178290303c14eae81","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/commits/fdd28399dc9da913a12983b178290303c14eae81/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/git/commits/fdd28399dc9da913a12983b178290303c14eae81","author":{"date":"2023-05-23T17:29:11.000-07:00","name":"Devashish Shankar","email":"devashish@meta.com"},"committer":{"date":"2023-05-24T16:43:32.000Z","name":"PyTorch MergeBot","email":"pytorchmergebot@users.noreply.github.com"},"message":"Replace unsqueeze transform with stack (#101766)\n\nAs part of split-cat transforms, we needed to unsqueeze additional inputs (not coming from split) but going to the cat/stack nodes.\n\nHowever, this leads to patterns like:\n\n```\nsplit -> unsqueeze -> cat\n```\n\nwhen there are multiple splits going into cat.\n\nAn alternative is to use stack rather than unsqueeze, leading to patterns like:\n\n```\nsplit -> stack -> cat\n```\n\nThis is much better, as repeated applications of the same pattern will further simplify \"split->stack\", which is not trivial in case of \"split->unsqueeze->cat\".\n\nAnother nice side-effect is lesser number of nodes in the graph overall.\n\nDifferential Revision: [D45952452](https://our.internmc.facebook.com/intern/diff/D45952452/)\n\nPull Request resolved: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/101766\nApproved by: https://github.com/jansel","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/git/trees/06a0a320fe62e8f2bbf3df66a3c76516f011f31f","sha":"06a0a320fe62e8f2bbf3df66a3c76516f011f31f"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"devashishshankar","id":980954,"node_id"